# Defect 451, 2026-10-08, the buffer beside the local. Symptom: C keeping
# the address of a buffer it was lent for one call and writing through it
# after the call had returned did so in silence, at exit 0 at `-O0`, `-O2`
# and under `--sanitize` at both (measured on this Mac at `56def9b4`).
# Cause: the buffer's region, given back at the call's end, was watched by
# nothing. Now its bytes are summed when it is given back and summed again
# when the program ends, and a sum that moved is named; under `--sanitize`
# the region is sealed and the write faults (`runtime/parts/lend.c`). The
# parameter is declared `lent`, and C kept the address all the same, which
# is the declaration's mistake about C.

extern "fixedbugs-451-keepers.h"
    function bytes_keep32(@md: [u8] counted_by 32 lent) -> i32
    function bytes_write_later() -> i64

function fill() -> i64
    md: [u8] @ []
    _ = bytes_keep32(@md)
    return md.len()

function main()
    print(fill())
    print(bytes_write_later())
